- **`crates/vox-code-audit/src/detectors/cross_crate_dup.rs`**: New batch detector identifies functions with byte-identical normalized bodies across different crates, flagging potential split-brain issues. It skips platform-sibling crates and trivial bodies to reduce false positives.
- **`crates/vox-code-audit/src/detectors/catch_all_swallow.rs`**: New per-file AST detection rule flags `match` expressions where a wildcard arm (`_ =>`) returns a neutral/empty value (e.g., `None`, `Vec::new()`, `Default::default()`) while explicit arms perform real work, indicating a silent value drop.
- **`crates/vox-code-audit/src/detectors/mod.rs`**: Registered `CatchAllSwallowDetector` and added `cross_crate_dup` and `catch_all_swallow` modules. The total rule count increased from 51 to 52.
